<opsproc code="00009120.0001001" revdate="2017-11-21T10:06:00"><title>Power Transfer Unit (<abb>PTU</abb>)</title><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.004"><title>After engine start</title><procbody lid="N.00009120.0001001.005"><action-block lid="N.00009120.0001001.006"><title>Check of the <abb>PTU</abb> operation:</title><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.007" memory="false"><cr-action code="00009120.0001001.002"><challenge><tech-label type="pb-sw">GREEN ENG 1 PUMP</tech-label></challenge><response>OFF</response></cr-action></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.008" memory="false"><command code="00009120.0001001.003"><para layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.009">On the <tech-label type="s-page">HYD</tech-label>,
check that the green system pressure is correct.</para></command><comment code="00009120.0001001.004"><para layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.010">A correct pressure
is <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">3000</measure> (± <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">200</measure>).</para></comment></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.013" memory="false"><cr-action code="00009120.0001001.006"><challenge><tech-label type="pb-sw">GREEN ENG 1 PUMP</tech-label></challenge><response>On</response></cr-action></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.015" memory="false"><cr-action code="00009120.0001001.008"><challenge><tech-label type="pb-sw">YELLOW ENG 2 PUMP</tech-label></challenge><response>OFF</response></cr-action></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.016" memory="false"><cr-action code="00009120.0001001.009"><challenge><tech-label type="pb-sw">YELLOW ELEC PUMP</tech-label></challenge><response>Off</response></cr-action></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.022" memory="false"><command code="00009120.0001001.013"><para layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.023">On the <tech-label type="s-page">HYD</tech-label>,
check that the yellow system pressure is correct.</para></command><comment code="00009120.0001001.014"><para layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.024">A correct pressure
is <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">3000</measure> (± <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">200</measure>).</para></comment></action><action layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.026" memory="false"><cr-action code="00009120.0001001.016"><challenge><tech-label type="pb-sw">YELLOW ENG 2 PUMP</tech-label></challenge><response>On</response></cr-action></action></action-block><inform layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.027"><noteproc code="00009120.0001001.017" layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.028"><numlist code="00009120.0001001.018" format="NNP" layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.029"><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.030">The <abb>PTU</abb> pressurizes the system to a nominal value of <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">3000</measure> (± <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">200</measure>), but if no consumers are operated the pressure is
not constant. The <abb>PTU</abb> operates in a cycle which keeps the
pressure in the hydraulic systems between <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">2100</measure> and <measure category="Pressure" show-unit="true" system="US" unit="PSI">3200</measure>.</para></item><item layer="1"><para layer="1" lid="N.00009120.0001001.032">For passengers
comfort, the <abb>PTU</abb> may be set to OFF during the taxi after
landing provided that both engines hydraulic pumps are operative and
running. The <abb>PTU</abb> must be set back to AUTO before leaving
the aircraft.</para></item></numlist></noteproc></inform></procbody></procitem></opsproc>